// DMCCIL1.src            CCI IIDDetail Lines 
//  RefreshCCI is calling dmGO with param EDIT_ONLY which calls amgo2.src gmRecalc_ccilin_vfcc
//  
//    gmPGA_ok            Dmlib086.pkg   sCode must be valid f#6-33
//    gmPGA_groups_title
//    gmExit_done_rrec    dmccil1.pkg
// Purpose       :  
// Called By     :  dmcci1.src
// Input Params  :
// Uses  Modules : dmccil1.pkg  gmExit_part/rrec
//                    : amlib025.pkg    gmSet_b3line_uom
//                          : i2lib063   // gmGet_cadex_rate
//                          : i2lib064   // gmUse_alternate
//                    : DmLib024.pkg    cRrec_info
//                    : edlib009.pkg    get_data_element
//               : cCadUtil.pkg  -  Sima_Mif_Provisional_From_HsPgaPgm
//               : cCadUtil.pkg  -  Permit_Number_From_HsPgaPgm  HsPgaPgm.Permit_Number_ForCcilin  // 2024-11-01
//               : dmlib132.pkg  -  autorate     
//               : dmlib086.pkg  -  pga    stuff
//               : amlib126.pkg  -  DocView        
//               : cSwInfo.pkg   -  cSwInfo       
//               : @CALL_PROGRAM_EXPORT_ONLY "AMCCILWH" - warehouse stuff
//               : zmlnfi3  popup b3line code
//               : @call_program "CCFTN1 INSERT_LINE"   ccftn1.src in AppSrcOO
// Calls Modules : amra1   rrec popup program
//               : dmacln1.src   F8-B3line updatecCadUtil.pkg  -  Permit_Number_From_HsPgaPgm  HsPgaPgm.Permit_Number_ForCcilin  // 2024-11-01
//               : dmCcxtSw.src  List and Update CcXtraSw
//               : dmUomIF.src 
//               : CdCodeFi.src     CadCode
// Question1     : How does the CcXtraSw list in dmCcxtSw get set?
// Answer1       : at Enter.Postsave if (giNewline_added)
//               :    calls mCopy_RrXtraSw_to_CcXtraSw in dmLib024.pkg
// Question2     : How does the Ratitem info get copied to ciilin 
// Notes         :
//               : ccilin is augmented by f#133 ccxtra
//               :        ref is 9 chars   5-{ccimasId} 2-{ccilinId}  2-subRef
//               :        ref is 9 chars   7-{ccilinId}               2-subRef  (airs and tvin)
//               :        ref is 7 chars   7-{ccilinId}  for prod
//               :        Type Description
//               :        AREG airs registration info  max 30 per ccilin
//               :        TVIN tc vehicle info         max ?  per ccilin  - still entered the "old" way
//               :        PROD make and model info for nrcan   - 1 per ccilin
//               :
//               : rating and ratitem are augmented by ratogd
//               :
//               : mSet_from_rrec# in dmLib024.pkg cRrec_Info   [++++ Nobody calls this ++++]
//               :     Called when adding a new CciLin right after the Rating Record / Ratitem is selected.
//               :     Sets fields on the CciLine entry screens with info from Rating and Ratitem
//               : 
//               : ccilin/b3line.pga_auto  (Y/N/blank)     +++++ OS +++++ get rid of blank for future stuff. ++++ OS ++++
//               :      Two uses:
//               :         .1. Accepting entry on the three fields s_pgaqa_list s_pgapgm_list s_sima
//               :                 blank acts like Y allowing entry on just one field s_pgaqa_list
//               :         .2. Setting automatically from rating
//               :                 blank acts like a N not setting the fields automatically
//               :          
// CAD Info      : CAD rule: Each Cci Line has its own unique B3line Code
//               : Uses cCadUtil.pkg for  Sima_Mif_Provisional_From_HsPgaPgm 

// Update_B3line : Send UpdateB3line_From_CadInfo   Enter1.Save Enter2.Save
//               : Send UpdateB3line_From_SimaInfo  Enter1.Save ENTER3.Save

// HsPgaPgm Info : Sima_Mif_Provisional_From_HsPgaPgm in cCadUtil.pkg sets ccilin.Sima_Mif_Provisional from HsPgaPgm.Sima_Mif_Provisional 
//               : Permit_Number_From_HsPgaPgm        in cCadUtil.pkg sets ccilin.Permit_Number        from HsPgaPgm.Permit_Number_ForCcilin  
//               :   only once when new ccilin is added. Using ccilin.PgaCode_List checking each PgaCode in list to HsPgaPgm 

// PGA Info      : ------------ Pga Columns in B3line and Ccilin ----------
//               : ++++ Secret Keyproc   Key.calculate (F5) outputs the calc screen dmPgaScn.pkg to notepad
//               :  Columns in both B3line and Ccilin
//               :   Pga_Auto                  Ogd_Group_Auto
//               :   PgaPgm_List               PgaPgm_List  
//               :   Sima                      Sima         
//               :   PgaQA_List                PgaQA_List   
//               :   PgaQA_Status              PgaQA_Status 
//               :  Pga1  Pga2  Pga3  Pga4  - not used anymore   Ogd_Group1  Ogd_Group2  Ogd_Group3  Ogd_Group4
//               : --------- B3line Pga Info - Usage ---------
//               :  The b3line Pga info is copied to ccilin screen fields
//               :    . when a new ccilin is added
//               :    . when an existing ccilin changes its line code
//               : --------------- B3line Pga Info Processing - not much -----------------
//               : Nothing happens in B3line Code (dmaclin1.src) if info is changed manually
//               : ie it does NOT get copied to ccilin in any bulk update                   
//               :    [unless ccilin.ogd_group_auto is Y, then it does - NO not done]  ???---????---????
//               :  All info is set from the last Ccilin updated
//               :     whether Pga_Auto is Y or N
//               :
//               : ---------------- Ccilin Pga Info Processing ----------
//               : .1. New b3line code:
//               :      Pga info set from:
//               :         . calc modules
//               : .2. New ccilin, after getting a line code
//               :             or existing ccilin, assigned a different line code
//               :     Pga info copied from B3line to Ccilin   --- copied from b3line ----
//               :     Pga info copiedf from rating / ratitem
//               : .3. All ccilin processing
//               :      Pga_Auto is Y
//               :                    .1. Generate PgaPgm_List_BeforeQA
//               :                    .2. Ensure PgaQA contains all questions
//               :                    .3. Ensure all Questions have answers and Q/A valid
//               :                    .4. Generate PgaPgm_List                   
//               :      Pga_Auto is N
//               :                    .1. 
//               :                    .2.                                      
//               :                    .3. Ensure all Questions have answers and Q/A valid
//               :                    .4.                           
//               :
//               : --------------------- mCopy_RrXtraSw_CcXtraSw1 in dmLib024.pkg -------
//               : mCopy_RrXtraSw_CcXtraSw1
//               :        1. New CcXtraSw for CciLn from RrXtraSw
//               :        2. If NAD - create new NAD for BACF from NAD for Opcust in RrXtraSw
//               :              uses gfCopyNad_CustToBacf in iid_cm.pkg
//               :              NAD if SwProcId.Code is NAD-
//               :        3. If LPCO (RrXtraSw.Process_Id = "SG121.LPCO")
//               :           fLpco_From_RrXtraSw_To_CcXtraSw                
//               :                Either use existing one for this Bacf or create a new one for this Bacf
//               :                fLpco_Use_Existing 
//               :                       Use existing one if:
//               :                          1. Lpco.type -> t#6-34 Help2 1PERSHIP
//               :                               . Look for existing one anywhere in Bacf same type. Use it if found.
//               :                          2. Lpco.Dif_Urn14 If not blank look for same. Use it if found.

//               :                          3. Lpco.type Look for existing one or more
//               :                                fLpco_Pick_Existing_Same_Type 
//               :                                     Count same type. 
//               :                                         If zero, return 0 so it will Add a new one               
//               :                                         If not zero, call Pick from list of existing and rating one  
//               :                 Add a new LPCO this bacf, adding one or two NADs
//               :

//This Constant is used in the title bar to show the version of dmccil1
